# Testing disabled (until further human notice)

Do **not** run, write, edit, or “verify in browser” any tests for this project until the human explicitly re-enables testing.

## Forbidden until re-enabled

- Opening or navigating a browser / Playwright MCP (`browser_navigate`, `browser_run_code_*`, snapshots for proof, etc.)
- Starting `python3 -m http.server` (or similar) **for** suite / smoke / click-proof
- Opening `tests/run.html`, running `tests/playwright-*.js`, or any suite / harness case
- Adding or editing files under `tests/` (cases, harness helpers, smoke scripts)
- Using Glass / inline browser to “confirm” a feature unless the human asks to see it

## Allowed

- Feature code changes only
- Updating `loop-tasks.md` status/conclusions without suite proof
- Human playtests the game themselves

## Where this ban is also recorded

- `loop-tasks.md` process banner (top) and **§14 Tests / QA** (`[blocked]` suite-proof rows)
- `README.md` → Tests section
- `loop-next.md` header (do not follow Test/URL lines while disabled)
- Agent todo `no-tests`
